-- New Hampshire had one stop.
--
-- Twenty-five categories needed adding, and the interesting ones were decided
-- by the single stop carrying them: 'secret-societies' is a Dartmouth
-- society's tomb room, 'magic-history' is a magician's grave, and
-- 'seasonal-oddities' is the Ice Castles, rebuilt every winter.
--
-- Better sourced than most — nhstateparks.org and visitnh.gov are both in the
-- top three, so a good share of these link somewhere a traveller can use.
--
-- Note the UFO cluster: five stops for the Betty and Barney Hill abduction
-- and the Exeter incident. New Hampshire is where American UFO folklore got
-- its shape, and this is the first state where ufos is not the smallest
-- category by a distance.
--
-- 110 stops, every one with a source.

insert into public.stops
  (name, slug, category, latitude, longitude, city, state, description,
   public_access, source, website, timezone, verified_at)
values
  ('Betty and Barney Hill Incident Historical Marker', 'betty-and-barney-hill-incident-historical-marker', 'ufos', 44.08547, -71.68413, 'Lincoln', 'NH', 'A state historical marker on U.S. Route 3 commemorates the 1961 experience reported by Betty and Barney Hill, who said they encountered a strange craft while driving through the White Mountains. Their later account became one of the most influential alleged alien-abduction stories in American popular culture. The marker gives OddWay travelers a concrete route point tied directly to the story.', 'roadside', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Notch Express Alien Abduction Display', 'notch-express-alien-abduction-display', 'ufos', 44.06418, -71.68695, 'Lincoln', 'NH', 'This otherwise ordinary roadside convenience store has embraced the Betty and Barney Hill story with an alien mural, newspaper clippings, photographs and UFO-related material. The result feels like a tiny roadside museum hidden inside a gas station. It is a separate stop from the nearby state historical marker.', 'open', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', 'https://www.loc8nearme.com/new-hampshire/lincoln/notch-express/6382355/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Graves of Betty and Barney Hill', 'graves-of-betty-and-barney-hill', 'ufos', 42.94318, -71.05854, 'Kingston', 'NH', 'Betty and Barney Hill are buried together in Greenwood Cemetery, far from the White Mountain road where their famous encounter was said to have occurred. Their shared grave has become a pilgrimage point for people interested in UFO history and the couple''s unusual place in American folklore. Visit respectfully and only during lawful cemetery access.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/betty-and-barney-hill-graves', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Exeter Incident Site', 'exeter-incident-site', 'ufos', 42.981, -70.948, 'Kensington', 'NH', 'In September 1965, teenager Norman Muscarello reported a large object with flashing red lights near Route 150 outside Exeter. Police officers later said they also observed unexplained lights, and journalist John G. Fuller''s book "Incident at Exeter" helped turn the case into a classic of American UFO history. The original area is now developed/private land, so this is a roadside history stop only. Secondary source: https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', 'roadside', 'https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2015-09-03/50-years-later-the-incident-at-exeter-still-fascinates-ufo-enthusiasts', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Betty and Barney Hill Archive', 'betty-and-barney-hill-archive', 'ufos', 43.13551, -70.93323, 'Durham', 'NH', 'UNH''s Milne Special Collections at Dimond Library preserves the Betty and Barney Hill Papers, including journals, correspondence, photographs, recordings, Betty''s dress and other material connected to their reported encounter and later UFO research. The collection is open for research by appointment rather than as a walk-in exhibit. Special Collections currently requires advance appointments. Secondary source: https://innovation.unh.edu/unh-innovation-spotlight-betty-barney-hill-collection', 'limited', 'https://library.unh.edu/find/archives/collections', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('America''s Stonehenge', 'americas-stonehenge', 'folklore', 42.84379, -71.20574, 'Salem', 'NH', 'Formerly known as Mystery Hill, this wooded property contains stone chambers, walls and standing stones that have inspired claims of ancient ceremonial builders and pre-Columbian European visitors. Those dramatic interpretations are disputed, and archaeologists have also connected much of the site to historic-era land use and later reconstruction. Whatever its origin, the maze of stone structures remains one of New Hampshire''s defining mystery attractions.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/americas-stonehenge', 'https://www.stonehengeusa.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Purgatory Falls and the Devil''s Bean Pot', 'purgatory-falls-and-the-devils-bean-pot', 'folklore', 42.88671, -71.70856, 'Lyndeborough', 'NH', 'Local folklore says the Devil once tried to cook beans beside the falls and left behind a large pothole known as the Devil''s Bean Pot along with a nearby footprint-like impression in the rock. The actual landscape is a series of waterfalls and sculpted bedrock reached by hiking trails. The folklore gives an already unusual natural site a distinctly OddWay story.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/purgatory-falls', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Eunice "Goody" Cole Memorial Stone', 'eunice-goody-cole-memorial-stone', 'folklore', 42.93344, -70.83482, 'Hampton', 'NH', 'Eunice "Goody" Cole was repeatedly accused of witchcraft in seventeenth-century Hampton and became one of the best-known witchcraft figures in New Hampshire history. A memorial stone on the town green acknowledges the accusations and the strange local legends that continued long after her death. It is a concrete stop tied to one of the state''s strongest witch-lore stories.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/eunice-goody-cole-memorial-stone', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Moulton Mansion', 'moulton-mansion', 'folklore', 42.93277, -70.8401, 'Hampton', 'NH', 'The old Moulton property is connected to one of Hampton''s most enduring legends: General Jonathan Moulton supposedly promised the Devil his soul in exchange for having his boots filled with gold, then tried to cheat the bargain by cutting holes in the boots. Later versions of the tale add a mysterious fire and the disappearance of Moulton''s wife. The surviving property is private, so view only from lawful public areas. Secondary source: https://www.hampton.lib.nh.us/hampton/history/moulton/legend.htm', 'private', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/moulton-mansion', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('The 1723 James House', 'the-1723-james-house', 'haunted', 42.94194, -70.86222, 'Hampton', 'NH', 'One of Hampton''s oldest surviving houses has developed a reputation for unexplained footsteps, laughter, slamming doors and other reported activity. The organization that preserves the property has hosted paranormal programs and investigations rather than distancing itself from the folklore. Visits should be made through scheduled openings or authorized events.', 'limited', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', 'https://jameshousemuseum.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('The Windham Restaurant', 'the-windham-restaurant', 'haunted', 42.80613, -71.26212, 'Windham', 'NH', 'This restaurant occupies a historic building that has accumulated stories of apparitions, footsteps and unexplained activity. Its ghost lore has been publicized alongside the building''s long local history, making it one of New Hampshire''s easier haunted stops to visit without joining a special tour. It remains an operating restaurant.', 'open', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', 'https://www.windhamrestaurant.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Madame Sherri''s Castle Ruins', 'madame-sherris-castle-ruins', 'weird-history', 42.86474, -72.51909, 'Chesterfield', 'NH', 'Costume designer Antoinette Sherri built an extravagant country estate here and became locally famous for lavish parties and eccentric behavior. The house burned in 1962, leaving stone foundations, columns and the remains of a dramatic staircase in the forest. The upper portion of the staircase collapsed in 2021, so visitors should admire the ruins without climbing them.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/madame-sherris-castle', 'https://www.chesterfield-conservation-commission.com/madame-sherri-forest', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Monson Center Ghost Town', 'monson-center-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 42.8354, -71.695, 'Milford', 'NH', 'Monson was an early inland colonial settlement established in the 1730s and abandoned only a few decades later for reasons that remain debated. Today a Forest Society reservation preserves cellar holes, old roads, stone walls and marked homestead sites along roughly three miles of trails. Unlike many alleged ghost towns, this one is specifically protected for public exploration.', 'open', 'https://www.forestsociety.org/property/monson-center', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Livermore Ghost Town', 'livermore-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 44.07451, -71.3773, 'Livermore', 'NH', 'Livermore grew as a White Mountain logging company town in the late nineteenth century before fires, floods and changing timber economics helped empty it. Foundations, cellar holes and traces of the settlement remain along Sawyer River Road. The road is seasonal and may be gated, but the former village can be explored on foot without trespassing on the nearby private camp. Secondary source: https://ournewenglandlegends.com/podcast-439-the-ghost-town-of-livermore/', 'limited', 'https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2017-07-21/you-asked-we-answered-what-happened-to-the-people-in-that-n-h-ghost-town', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Willey House Historic Site', 'willey-house-historic-site', 'weird-history', 44.16646, -71.38563, 'Hart''s Location', 'NH', 'The Willey family lived beneath the steep walls of Crawford Notch when a catastrophic landslide struck in August 1826. Their house was miraculously spared by the debris, but the entire family and two hired men died after apparently fleeing it. The tragedy became one of the White Mountains'' most famous nineteenth-century disaster stories. Secondary source: https://www.topozone.com/new-hampshire/carroll-nh/locale/willey-house/', 'limited', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/crawford-notch-state-park', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Omni Mount Washington Resort — Princess Carolyn Ghost', 'omni-mount-washington-resort-princess-carolyn-ghost', 'haunted', 44.25843, -71.43985, 'Bretton Woods', 'NH', 'The grand 1902 Mount Washington Hotel is associated with stories of Carolyn Stickney, whose apparition is said to appear in Victorian clothing and who is often nicknamed "the Princess." Room 314, once part of her private suite, is particularly tied to the hotel''s ghost lore. The property remains an operating resort, so paranormal interest should not interfere with guests.', 'open', 'https://www.historichotels.org/us/hotels-resorts/omni-mount-washington-resort/ghost-stories.php', 'https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/bretton-woods-mount-washington', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Newport Opera House', 'newport-opera-house', 'haunted', 43.3646, -72.17265, 'Newport', 'NH', 'The historic Newport Opera House has been investigated by paranormal groups after reports of unexplained sounds, shadowy figures and unusual experiences inside the building. Its preserved stage and upper-level spaces give the stories a strong physical setting. Access is through performances, events and authorized tours rather than unrestricted exploration.', 'limited', 'https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2023-10-27/newport-opera-house-ghosts-paranormal-new-hampshire', 'https://newportoperahouse.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Woodman Museum Oddities', 'woodman-museum-oddities', 'museums', 43.18969, -70.8747, 'Dover', 'NH', 'The Woodman Museum is an old-fashioned local museum packed with the kind of objects that rarely survive modern exhibit design. Its collections have included taxidermy, a four-legged chicken, a man-eating clam shell, military artifacts and other curiosities spread through several historic buildings. Seasonal hours make this a check-ahead stop. Secondary source: https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/21104', 'limited', 'https://woodmanmuseum.org/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('American Classic Arcade Museum', 'american-classic-arcade-museum', 'museums', 43.61298, -71.47748, 'Laconia', 'NH', 'Hidden inside Funspot is a museum devoted to the golden age of coin-operated video games. Roughly 180 classic machines from the 1970s and 1980s are displayed at a time, with additional games rotated from storage. The combination of museum preservation and functioning arcade floor makes it far more interactive than a typical technology exhibit.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/american-classic-arcade-museum', 'https://www.classicarcademuseum.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('New Hampshire Telephone Museum', 'new-hampshire-telephone-museum', 'museums', 43.27984, -71.81503, 'Warner', 'NH', 'This museum traces the evolution of telephones through switchboards, early handsets, novelty phones and communications equipment that spans generations. Many exhibits emphasize the physical machinery that once connected calls before digital networks made it invisible. Public hours are seasonal, so check the current calendar. Secondary source: https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/5-odd-museums', 'limited', 'https://www.nhtelephonemuseum.org/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Extreme Mount Washington', 'extreme-mount-washington', 'roadside-oddities', 44.27059, -71.30327, 'Sargent''s Purchase', 'NH', 'Inside the Sherman Adams Visitor Center at the summit of Mount Washington, this museum recreates the extreme weather that made the mountain famous. Exhibits cover the observatory, brutal wind, cold and the 231-mph gust measured here in 1934. Reaching the museum requires reaching the summit by hiking, the Auto Road or the Cog Railway, and seasonal mountain access can change rapidly.', 'limited', 'https://www.nhsgc.sr.unh.edu/about.html', 'https://mountwashington.org/about-us/visit-us/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Ruggles Mine', 'ruggles-mine', 'weird-history', 43.58966, -71.99455, 'Grafton', 'NH', 'This enormous former mica mine cuts open the side of Isinglass Mountain with tunnels, pits and mineral-rich rock faces. After years of closure, Ruggles reopened to the public and again allows visitors to explore and collect a limited amount of minerals under site rules. The 2026 season is scheduled to run through October 11.', 'limited', 'https://www.rugglesmine.net/', 'https://www.rugglesmine.net/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('USS Albacore', 'uss-albacore', 'roadside-oddities', 43.08225, -70.76696, 'Portsmouth', 'NH', 'USS Albacore was an experimental submarine whose streamlined hull helped shape later generations of U.S. Navy submarines. The vessel now sits permanently on land, allowing visitors to climb inside its cramped compartments and control spaces. The museum operates most of the year but closes during part of the winter.', 'limited', 'https://www.ussalbacore.org/', 'https://www.ussalbacore.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Hannah Duston Memorial', 'hannah-duston-memorial', 'weird-history', 43.28816, -71.59071, 'Boscawen', 'NH', 'A 35-foot monument commemorates Hannah Duston, who was taken captive during King William''s War in 1697 and later killed ten Abenaki people at a camp before escaping. The nineteenth-century monument presents one version of a violent colonial story whose interpretation has become increasingly contested. The state historic site is currently listed as always open for recreation.', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/hannah-duston-memorial-historic-site', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Andres Institute of Art Sculpture Park', 'andres-institute-of-art-sculpture-park', 'roadside-oddities', 42.72813, -71.66877, 'Brookline', 'NH', 'More than 100 large-scale sculptures are scattered through roughly 140 acres of wooded hiking trails on Potanipo Hill. The pieces appear unexpectedly among rocks, trees and former ski-area terrain, turning the mountain into an outdoor gallery that feels more like a scavenger hunt than a conventional museum. Trails are open daily from dawn to dusk.', 'open', 'https://andresinstitute.org/visit/', 'https://andresinstitute.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles Birthplace Marker', 'teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-birthplace-marker', 'roadside-oddities', 43.18942, -70.87109, 'Dover', 'NH', 'Kevin Eastman and Peter Laird created the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles in Dover in 1983, sketching the first turtle as a joke before developing the idea into a comic. A public marker and themed manhole cover now commemorate the city''s unexpected role in launching the franchise. It is a compact but legitimate pop-culture pilgrimage stop.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-birthplace', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Old Man of the Mountain Profile Plaza', 'old-man-of-the-mountain-profile-plaza', 'weird-history', 44.16568, -71.67882, 'Franconia', 'NH', 'New Hampshire''s famous Old Man of the Mountain rock profile collapsed from Cannon Cliff in 2003. At Profile Plaza, steel "profilers" allow visitors to stand at specific points and visually reconstruct the vanished face against the cliff. The memorial turns an absent landmark into something visitors can still physically line up and see. Secondary source: https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=81875', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/franconia-notch-state-park', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Redstone Missile', 'redstone-missile', 'roadside-oddities', 43.95877, -71.90769, 'Warren', 'NH', 'A full-size Redstone missile stands improbably in a small New Hampshire town park. The missile type was originally developed as a ballistic weapon and later adapted to launch Alan Shepard, the New Hampshire-born first American in space. Its towering presence beside ordinary village surroundings makes it one of the state''s strongest roadside oddities.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/redstone-rocket', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Memorial Arch of Tilton', 'memorial-arch-of-tilton', 'roadside-oddities', 43.44049, -71.58881, 'Northfield', 'NH', 'Industrialist Charles E. Tilton built this massive Roman-style stone arch as a memorial to his ancestors. It stands high above the Winnipesaukee River and looks wildly oversized for the rural hilltop around it. A short trail leads visitors to the monument and surrounding views.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/memorial-arch-of-tilton', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Benson Park Gorilla Cage', 'benson-park-gorilla-cage', 'weird-history', 42.76924, -71.40278, 'Hudson', 'NH', 'Benson''s Wild Animal Farm once drew crowds with elephants, lions, gorillas and other animals before closing in 1987. The land is now a public park, but several structures from the attraction remain, including the distinctive former gorilla cage that visitors can walk into. It is an unusually intact fragment of a vanished roadside zoo.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/bensons-animal-park', 'https://www.hudsonnh.gov/bensonpark', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Polar Caves', 'polar-caves', 'roadside-oddities', 43.7812, -71.78112, 'Rumney', 'NH', 'Glacial boulders piled against one another here to form narrow passages, chambers and squeezes with names such as the Lemon Squeezer and Devil''s Turnpike. Unlike a traditional limestone cavern, these "caves" are spaces between enormous granite blocks left by glacial activity. The attraction is ticketed and seasonal.', 'limited', 'https://polarcaves.com/', 'https://polarcaves.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Sculptured Rocks Natural Area', 'sculptured-rocks-natural-area', 'roadside-oddities', 43.70716, -71.85465, 'Groton', 'NH', 'The Cockermouth River has carved deep potholes, bowls and smooth twisting channels into the bedrock here over thousands of years. The shapes look almost intentionally sculpted, which gives the gorge its name. The state natural area is generally open for recreation, though conditions can become hazardous around high water and ice.', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/sculptured-rocks-natural-area', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('The Basin', 'the-basin', 'roadside-oddities', 44.12108, -71.68295, 'Lincoln', 'NH', 'A powerful whirlpool of water and stone carved this large, smooth granite pothole at the foot of a cascade in Franconia Notch. Nineteenth-century visitors compared its near-perfect rounded walls to an enormous natural basin. It is reached by a short public trail from the parkway. Secondary source: https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-basin', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/franconia-notch-state-park', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('The Chocorua Legend Historical Marker', 'the-chocorua-legend-historical-marker', 'folklore', 43.90887, -71.23431, 'Tamworth', 'NH', 'A state marker summarizes the legend of Chocorua, whose death on the mountain was later embellished into stories of revenge and a curse upon local settlers. Multiple versions disagree about what actually happened, and even the historical identity behind the legend is debated. The marker provides a concrete roadside point for a story that otherwise spreads across an entire mountain.', 'roadside', 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=152078', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Wallace Horse Cemetery', 'wallace-horse-cemetery', 'weird-history', 44.29677, -71.77234, 'Littleton', 'NH', 'This tiny fenced cemetery is dedicated to three Morgan horses, Maud, Mollie and Maggie, that belonged to Eli and Myra Wallace. The horses were buried with equipment including harnesses, bridles, blankets and feed boxes, and Wallace''s estate provided for the site''s continued care. It is one of New England''s most unusual purpose-built animal cemeteries. Secondary source: https://www.visitwhitemountains.com/blog/post/scary-tales-of-the-white-mountains/', 'open', 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/31777', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Chutters — 112-Foot Candy Counter', 'chutters-112-foot-candy-counter', 'roadside-oddities', 44.30651, -71.77199, 'Littleton', 'NH', 'Chutters'' downtown store contains a candy counter stretching 112 feet along the shop, once recognized by Guinness as the world''s longest. Rows of jars and bins turn an ordinary candy shop into a deliberately excessive roadside attraction. The business is currently open seven days a week.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/chutters-candy-store', 'https://www.chutters.com/littleton', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Madison Boulder', 'madison-boulder', 'roadside-oddities', 43.93121, -71.16797, 'Madison', 'NH', 'Madison Boulder is an enormous glacial erratic carried and deposited by moving ice during the last Ice Age. The exposed granite block is roughly the size of a small building and has long been promoted as one of the largest known glacial erratics in New England. A short approach makes the scale easy to appreciate from ground level.', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/madison-boulder-natural-area', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Orozco''s "The Epic of American Civilization"', 'orozcos-the-epic-of-american-civilization', 'roadside-oddities', 43.7052, -72.28897, 'Hanover', 'NH', 'Mexican muralist José Clemente Orozco covered the walls of Dartmouth''s Baker-Berry Library reserve corridor with a dark, violent and often surreal interpretation of the history of the Americas. Gods, skeletons, machinery, conquest and war fill the panels rather than the genteel imagery expected in an Ivy League library. Public viewing follows current library access policies. Secondary source: https://www.nps.gov/places/orozco-murals.htm', 'limited', 'https://hoodmuseum.dartmouth.edu/explore/oorozco-mural', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Ponemah Bog Boardwalk', 'ponemah-bog-boardwalk', 'roadside-oddities', 42.8167, -71.5883, 'Amherst', 'NH', 'A boardwalk enters a floating bog landscape filled with sphagnum, pitcher plants, sundews and other species adapted to acidic wetland conditions. The environment can feel more like a northern peatland than suburban southern New Hampshire. Visitors should remain on the boardwalk to protect the fragile habitat.', 'open', 'https://www.nhaudubon.org/lands/sanctuaries/ponemah-bog/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Drowned Forest at Odiorne Point', 'drowned-forest-at-odiorne-point', 'folklore', 43.04529, -70.71411, 'Rye', 'NH', 'At sufficiently low tide, ancient tree stumps and root systems appear along the shore near Odiorne Point, remnants of a forest drowned as sea level changed thousands of years ago. The exposed wood creates the eerie impression of a forest floor emerging from the ocean. Visibility depends on tide and conditions, so this is not guaranteed on every visit. Secondary source: https://www.nhmagazine.com/explore-nhs-drowned-forest/', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/sunken-forests-rye-nh', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Fort Stark', 'fort-stark', 'weird-history', 43.05759, -70.71302, 'New Castle', 'NH', 'Concrete batteries and defensive structures overlook Portsmouth Harbor at this former coastal fort. The site combines abandoned-looking military architecture with a dramatic oceanfront setting, while interpretive material explains its role in the harbor defense system. Grounds and interior access can vary by season and restoration status.', 'limited', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/fort-stark-state-historic-site', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Pulpit Rock Tower', 'pulpit-rock-tower', 'weird-history', 43.03322, -70.72108, 'Rye', 'NH', 'This concrete World War II observation tower was part of the coastal fire-control network protecting Portsmouth Harbor. Its tall, windowed silhouette rises unexpectedly from the trees and looks more like a small brutalist castle than a military instrument. The exterior can be viewed from the site, while interior openings are limited and should be checked in advance.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/pulpit-rock-tower', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Graves of the Smuttynose Murder Victims', 'graves-of-the-smuttynose-murder-victims', 'weird-history', 43.06603, -70.75788, 'Portsmouth', 'NH', 'Matching gravestones in South Cemetery mark Karen Christensen and Anethe Christensen, two women murdered on Smuttynose Island in 1873. A third woman escaped and accused Louis Wagner, who was later executed for the killings, though debate over the case persisted. The graves provide a mainland stop tied directly to one of the Isles of Shoals'' darkest stories.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/graves-smuttynose-murder-victims', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Charlotte Gemmell''s Teacher''s Desk Tombstone', 'charlotte-gemmells-teachers-desk-tombstone', 'weird-history', 42.94841, -72.31561, 'Keene', 'NH', 'Teacher Charlotte Gemmell''s granite grave marker is carved as a school desk complete with books and an apple. The personalized monument looks startlingly literal among conventional cemetery stones. The coordinate routes to Monadnock View Cemetery; follow the cemetery''s posted hours and directions to locate the individual grave.', 'limited', 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/33927', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Emil Hanslin''s Loaf of Bread Tomb', 'emil-hanslins-loaf-of-bread-tomb', 'weird-history', 43.40479, -71.99064, 'New London', 'NH', 'An above-ground stone tomb in Old Main Street Cemetery looks uncannily like an enormous loaf of bread. Roadside lore has sometimes claimed Hanslin was a baker, but he was actually involved in real estate—the resemblance appears to be coincidental. That lack of an elaborate legend arguably makes the oversized stone form stranger.', 'limited', 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/8519', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Grave of Sevilla Jones', 'grave-of-sevilla-jones', 'weird-history', 42.97296, -71.68825, 'New Boston', 'NH', 'Seventeen-year-old Sevilla Jones was murdered by Henry Sargent in 1854 while walking to school. Her unusually blunt gravestone names Sargent as her killer and describes the shooting, turning the marker into a permanent public accusation. Sargent is buried only a short distance away in the same cemetery.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/grave-of-sevilla-jones', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Ralph Baer Memorial', 'ralph-baer-memorial', 'roadside-oddities', 42.99333, -71.46777, 'Manchester', 'NH', 'A bronze statue of inventor Ralph Baer sits on a bench in Arms Park near the Manchester mill buildings where he developed pioneering home video-game technology. Baer is widely credited as the "father of the video game" for work that led to the Magnavox Odyssey. Visitors can sit beside the life-size figure overlooking the Merrimack River.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ralph-baer-memorial', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Grave of Christa McAuliffe', 'grave-of-christa-mcauliffe', 'weird-history', 43.22357, -71.55551, 'Concord', 'NH', 'Concord teacher Christa McAuliffe was selected for NASA''s Teacher in Space Project and died with the crew of Space Shuttle Challenger in 1986. Her grave remains in Concord and is part of the city''s enduring connection to her life and legacy. Visit respectfully during cemetery hours; the grave is in Block M, Lot 51L.', 'limited', 'https://www.concordmonitor.com/2026/01/29/christa-mcauliffe-legacy-concord/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Haunted Margaritas — Former Concord Jail', 'haunted-margaritas-former-concord-jail', 'haunted', 43.20496, -71.53663, 'Concord', 'NH', 'This Margaritas restaurant occupies Concord''s former police station and jail, and several old cells remain incorporated into the dining area. Local ghost stories describe a presence nicknamed "George," and paranormal investigators have visited the building. Even without the haunting claims, eating inside preserved jail cells makes it an unusually tangible stop.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/haunted-margaritas', 'https://www.margs.com/locations/concord/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Lake Winnipesaukee Mystery Stone', 'lake-winnipesaukee-mystery-stone', 'folklore', 43.20727, -71.53943, 'Concord', 'NH', 'This polished, egg-shaped stone was reportedly found near Lake Winnipesaukee in 1872 and is carved with a face, geometric designs and other symbols. Its maker and purpose have inspired more than a century of theories, though the precisely drilled holes have led some researchers to suspect a nineteenth-century origin rather than an ancient artifact. The stone is preserved by the New Hampshire Historical Society in Concord.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/lake-winnipesaukee-mystery-stone', 'https://www.nhhistory.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Three Chimneys Inn', 'three-chimneys-inn', 'haunted', 43.13225, -70.91877, 'Durham', 'NH', 'Built in 1649, Three Chimneys Inn occupies one of the oldest surviving homes in New Hampshire and still operates as lodging. Local ghost lore centers on a presence called Hannah, said to be connected to a drowning in the Oyster River and blamed for unexplained disturbances involving electronics. The haunting is folklore, but the building itself is a legitimate historic inn visitors can stay in.', 'open', 'https://www.ci.durham.nh.us/fridayupdate/friday-updates-august-17th-2018', 'https://www.threechimneysinn.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Notchland Inn — Nancy Barton Ghost', 'notchland-inn-nancy-barton-ghost', 'haunted', 44.11528, -71.35556, 'Hart''s Location', 'NH', 'The Notchland Inn sits near the setting of one of the White Mountains'' enduring ghost stories. Nancy Barton reportedly died in 1778 while searching the winter wilderness for her missing fiancé, and later folklore describes her spirit wandering the area around the old road and inn property. The inn remains an operating lodging property, so visitors should respect guests and private areas.', 'open', 'https://ournewenglandlegends.com/podcast-191-the-ghost-of-nancy-barton/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Tilton Inn', 'tilton-inn', 'haunted', 43.44252, -71.58833, 'Tilton', 'NH', 'This historic inn has survived multiple fires and accumulated stories of unexplained footsteps, apparitions and other paranormal activity. One of the best-known legends concerns a young girl named Laura, while the Sanborn Room has also been singled out in ghost stories and investigations. It remains an active inn and restaurant rather than a dedicated haunted attraction.', 'open', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/blog/undiscovered-nh-spooky-stops', 'https://www.thetiltoninn.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Grave of Ocean-Born Mary', 'grave-of-ocean-born-mary', 'folklore', 43.17532, -71.82204, 'Henniker', 'NH', 'Mary Wallace became known as "Ocean-Born Mary" because she was born aboard a ship crossing the Atlantic in 1720. Later storytellers transformed her life into tales involving pirates, hidden treasure and a supposedly haunted house, although much of that lore has been debunked. Her actual grave behind Henniker''s town hall gives travelers a concrete stop tied to the legend. Secondary source: https://newenglandhistoricalsociety.com/ocean-born-mary-new-hampshire-legend/', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ocean-born-mary', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Amos J. Blake House Museum', 'amos-j-blake-house-museum', 'haunted', 42.77998, -72.14557, 'Fitzwilliam', 'NH', 'The Fitzwilliam Historical Society preserves this nineteenth-century house as a local museum filled with period furnishings and artifacts. Staff and visitors have reported unexplained sounds, voices and other alleged activity, including stories of multiple spirits and even a phantom cat. Tours are currently arranged by appointment, so visitors should contact the museum in advance.', 'limited', 'https://www.verani.com/view-blog/wicked-spooky-spots-in-new-england-to-give-you-the-chills-this-halloween', 'https://www.fitzhistoric.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Pine Hill Cemetery — Blood Cemetery', 'pine-hill-cemetery-blood-cemetery', 'haunted', 42.7682, -71.53861, 'Hollis', 'NH', 'Pine Hill Cemetery is widely nicknamed Blood Cemetery because of the Blood family buried there, especially Abel Blood and a gravestone whose carved hand helped fuel local legends. Stories describe apparitions, strange lights and other activity around the burial ground, though these remain folklore. Visit only during lawful cemetery hours and treat the graves respectfully. Secondary source: https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/pine-hill-cemetery-blood-cemetery/', 'limited', 'https://www.nhmagazine.com/where-to-find-ghosts-ghouls-and-scares-in-the-granite-state/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Gilson Road Cemetery', 'gilson-road-cemetery', 'haunted', 42.71628, -71.513, 'Nashua', 'NH', 'This small historic cemetery has developed an outsized reputation among New Hampshire ghost hunters. Reported experiences include mist-like figures, a sensation compared with walking through water and sightings of a dark hooded form. The claims are unverified folklore, and the cemetery should be visited quietly and only during permitted hours.', 'limited', 'https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/gilson-road-cemetery/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Woodland Cemetery and Sumner Knight Chapel', 'woodland-cemetery-and-sumner-knight-chapel', 'haunted', 42.94322, -72.2686, 'Keene', 'NH', 'Woodland Cemetery''s stone chapel and surrounding graves have generated local stories about laughter, apparitions and a spirit that supposedly reacts to visitors who swear. The Sumner Knight Chapel gives the folklore a dramatic physical setting within the cemetery. Public cemetery access does not imply permission to enter locked buildings or conduct investigations after hours.', 'limited', 'https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/sumner-knight-chapel-woodland-cemetery/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Vale End Cemetery — Blue Lady', 'vale-end-cemetery-blue-lady', 'haunted', 42.8438, -71.77255, 'Wilton', 'NH', 'Vale End Cemetery is associated with the legend of a glowing female apparition called the Blue Lady, often linked in modern retellings to Mary Ritter Spaulding. The story has become one of southern New Hampshire''s better-known cemetery legends despite limited historical evidence for the supernatural claims. Visit during cemetery hours and avoid disturbing graves or neighboring property. Secondary source: https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/vale-end-cemetery/', 'limited', 'https://ournewenglandlegends.com/podcast-393-the-blue-lady-of-vale-end-cemetery/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Huntress Hall', 'huntress-hall', 'folklore', 42.92722, -72.27929, 'Keene', 'NH', 'Keene State College students have long passed around stories of wheelchair sounds and other unexplained activity inside Huntress Hall, often attributing them to Harriet Huntress. Historical timelines complicate the legend because Huntress died before the residence hall opened, making this a good example of campus folklore evolving independently of fact. The hall is an active residence, so OddWay visitors should view it only from public campus areas.', 'roadside', 'https://spookfinder.com/place/huntress-hall', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Haunted Overload', 'haunted-overload', 'haunted', 43.15699, -70.96663, 'Lee', 'NH', 'Haunted Overload transforms the woods of DeMeritt Hill Farm into a large-scale outdoor haunt filled with elaborate handmade sets, towering monsters and theatrical lighting. It has become one of New Hampshire''s best-known seasonal Halloween attractions. Admission is ticketed and operations are limited to the fall season.', 'limited', 'https://hauntedoverload.com/', 'https://hauntedoverload.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Fright Kingdom', 'fright-kingdom', 'haunted', 42.75151, -71.49023, 'Nashua', 'NH', 'Fright Kingdom is an indoor haunted attraction complex built around multiple themed environments, monsters and elaborate sets. The 2026 schedule includes its main Halloween season from late September through October with additional special events later in the year. Admission is ticketed and dates vary by event.', 'limited', 'https://frightkingdom.com/hours/', 'https://frightkingdom.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('SpookyWorld Presents Nightmare New England', 'spookyworld-presents-nightmare-new-england', 'haunted', 42.88052, -71.46828, 'Litchfield', 'NH', 'SpookyWorld and Nightmare New England combine several large haunted attractions on one property, including indoor haunts, outdoor trails and themed experiences. The operation traces its identity back to the influential SpookyWorld attraction that helped shape New England''s commercial haunted-house scene. It is ticketed and operates on selected dates during the Halloween season.', 'limited', 'https://www.nightmarenewengland.com/events', 'https://www.nightmarenewengland.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('GHOST LIGHT at Jean''s Playhouse', 'ghost-light-at-jeans-playhouse', 'haunted', 44.03999, -71.66851, 'Lincoln', 'NH', 'Jean''s Playhouse turns its theater into an immersive walk-through horror experience called GHOST LIGHT. The 2026 event is scheduled for selected nights from October 9 through October 31 and uses theatrical performers, sets and effects rather than a conventional stage show. Tickets and age recommendations should be checked before visiting.', 'limited', 'https://www.visitnh.gov/things-to-do/events-calendar/ghost-light-a-haunting-experience', 'https://jeansplayhouse.com/project/ghost-light/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Frog Rock', 'frog-rock', 'roadside-oddities', 42.93231, -71.72304, 'New Boston', 'NH', 'A massive split boulder in the woods resembles a crouching frog when viewed from the right angle. Frog Rock was once a well-known nineteenth-century scenic curiosity before changing roads and travel patterns left it comparatively obscure. The natural formation remains reachable on foot and makes a strong old-school roadside-oddity detour.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/frog-rock-new-hampshire', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Chester Village Cemetery Carved Faces', 'chester-village-cemetery-carved-faces', 'weird-history', 42.95773, -71.25568, 'Chester', 'NH', 'Chester Village Cemetery contains a striking group of eighteenth-century gravestones carved with unusually expressive human faces. Several are attributed to local stonecarvers Stephen and Abel Webster, whose work ranges from smiling heads to grim or almost cartoonish expressions. The stones are historical funerary art, so visitors should look without touching or rubbing them.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/chester-village-cemetery', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Captain Jones''s Leg Grave', 'captain-joness-leg-grave', 'weird-history', 43.17594, -72.10087, 'Washington', 'NH', 'After Captain Samuel Jones lost a leg to amputation in 1804, the severed limb reportedly received its own funeral and burial while Jones himself lived for years afterward. A marker preserves the bizarre story in Washington''s cemetery landscape. It is one of the state''s clearest examples of a literal grave for only part of a person.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/captain-jones-leg-grave', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Gravesite of Richard Potter', 'gravesite-of-richard-potter', 'weird-history', 43.43649, -71.85588, 'Andover', 'NH', 'Richard Potter, born in 1783, became one of the first American-born professional magicians and a prominent Black entertainer in the early United States. He and his wife Sally are buried near Potter Place, the village that eventually took his name. The graves are behind the historic railroad-station area and are accessible for respectful visits.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/gravesite-of-richard-potter-americas-first-professional-magician', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Claude Rains Grave', 'claude-rains-grave', 'weird-history', 43.72593, -71.47517, 'Moultonborough', 'NH', 'Actor Claude Rains, remembered for films including "The Invisible Man" and "Casablanca," is buried in Red Hill Cemetery. His grave and his wife''s are marked by distinctive polished black stones with an almost futuristic shape. The secluded New Hampshire burial site makes an unexpected film-history stop.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/claude-rains-grave', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('William G. Bruce''s Granite Dog Grave', 'william-g-bruces-granite-dog-grave', 'weird-history', 42.89453, -71.67424, 'Mont Vernon', 'NH', 'William G. Bruce died in a hunting accident, and his grave was given an unusually elaborate memorial featuring a life-size granite hunting dog. The animal appears to stand guard beside the marker long after Bruce''s death. Visit respectfully and only during permitted cemetery access.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/william-g-bruce-grave', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Caroline Cutter Headstone', 'caroline-cutter-headstone', 'weird-history', 42.83509, -71.65378, 'Milford', 'NH', 'Caroline Cutter''s gravestone carries an exceptionally long inscription placed there by her husband, who used the monument to accuse Baptist ministers and churches of contributing to her death. The result reads less like a conventional epitaph and more like a permanent public grievance carved into stone. It is located in Milford Cemetery.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/caroline-cutter-headstone', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Captain Sam Greele Monument', 'captain-sam-greele-monument', 'roadside-oddities', 42.82105, -71.78314, 'Wilton', 'NH', 'A roadside obelisk marks the place where Captain Samuel Greele was killed by a falling tree in 1798. Instead of moving the memorial into a cemetery or town square, later residents preserved the exact location of the freak accident. The monument is visible from the roadside but should be approached only where it is safe to pull off legally.', 'roadside', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/captain-sam-greele-monument', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Josie Langmaid Monument', 'josie-langmaid-monument', 'weird-history', 43.14727, -71.44611, 'Suncook', 'NH', 'A tall monument commemorates Josie Langmaid, a 17-year-old murdered in 1875 in a case that shocked New Hampshire. The inscription records unusually direct details of her death, making the memorial far more explicit than most nineteenth-century grave markers. Treat the site as a memorial to a victim rather than a novelty.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/josie-langmaid-monument', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Redstone Rocket Replica', 'redstone-rocket-replica', 'weird-history', 43.22416, -71.53259, 'Concord', 'NH', 'A 92-foot Redstone rocket replica towers outside the McAuliffe-Shepard Discovery Center. The Redstone family of rockets included the vehicle that launched New Hampshire native Alan Shepard on the first American crewed spaceflight. The outdoor rocket can be seen without entering the museum.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/redstone-rocket-replica', 'https://www.starhop.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Donkey Kong Mural', 'donkey-kong-mural', 'roadside-oddities', 43.20342, -71.5365, 'Concord', 'NH', 'A downtown mural transforms a tall elevator shaft into a giant level of the classic Donkey Kong arcade game. Painted in 2022, the work uses the building''s vertical shape as part of the joke, with pixel-style platforms climbing toward the roof. It is best viewed from public streets without entering the residential property.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/donkey-kong-mural', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Cat Alley', 'cat-alley', 'roadside-oddities', 42.99002, -71.46303, 'Manchester', 'NH', 'An otherwise ordinary pedestrian alley in downtown Manchester has been turned into a gallery of cat-themed murals. More than 20 painted cats appear in styles ranging from realistic portraits to pop-culture riffs. The public walkway is free and open year-round.', 'open', 'https://www.visitmanchesternh.com/things-to-do/cat-alley/', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Richard McDonald''s Niche', 'richard-mcdonalds-niche', 'weird-history', 43.0057, -71.48595, 'Manchester', 'NH', 'Richard McDonald, one of the brothers whose restaurant system became McDonald''s, is interred at Mount Calvary Cemetery in Manchester. His niche includes imagery referencing the Golden Arches and his role in the company''s history. The understated cemetery stop is an unusual endpoint for one of America''s most recognizable business stories.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/richard-mcdonalds-niche', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Harriet E. Wilson Memorial', 'harriet-e-wilson-memorial', 'weird-history', 42.83325, -71.64991, 'Milford', 'NH', 'A bronze memorial honors Harriet E. Wilson, author of the 1859 novel "Our Nig," a landmark work in African American literary history. Wilson was born in Milford and endured poverty and indentured servitude before becoming an author, lecturer and spiritualist. The statue stands in public Bicentennial Park.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/harriet-wilson-statue', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Endicott Rock', 'endicott-rock', 'weird-history', 43.60494, -71.45617, 'Laconia', 'NH', 'Protected beneath a small stone shelter is a boulder inscribed in 1652 during an early attempt to establish the northern boundary of Massachusetts. The marks are often described as among the oldest surviving public inscriptions or monuments of colonial government in New England. The state historic site is generally open for outdoor visitation unless otherwise posted.', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/endicott-rock-historic-site', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('1946 Nashua Dodgers Mural', '1946-nashua-dodgers-mural', 'weird-history', 42.75751, -71.46598, 'Nashua', 'NH', 'A large mural commemorates the 1946 Nashua Dodgers and players Roy Campanella and Don Newcombe. Their season in Nashua was an important early step in the integration of twentieth-century professional baseball before both men reached the major leagues. The artwork turns that history into an easily accessible downtown stop.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/1946-nashua-dodgers-mural', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Old Country Store and Museum', 'old-country-store-and-museum', 'museums', 43.75516, -71.39632, 'Moultonborough', 'NH', 'Operating in a building with roots dating to 1781, the Old Country Store combines a working general store with an upstairs collection of historical objects and curiosities. The densely packed rooms feel closer to an old cabinet of local oddities than a polished modern museum. The business currently operates year-round.', 'open', 'https://nhcountrystore.com/', 'https://nhcountrystore.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Castle in the Clouds', 'castle-in-the-clouds', 'roadside-oddities', 43.72061, -71.32245, 'Moultonborough', 'NH', 'The mountaintop mansion known as Lucknow was completed in the early twentieth century for industrialist Thomas Plant. Its Arts and Crafts design incorporated then-cutting-edge technology including unusual plumbing, refrigeration and electrical systems. The estate, trails and mansion are ticketed or seasonally operated depending on the area.', 'limited', 'https://www.castleintheclouds.org/hours-admission/', 'https://www.castleintheclouds.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Cathedral of the Pines', 'cathedral-of-the-pines', 'roadside-oddities', 42.77481, -71.98834, 'Rindge', 'NH', 'This outdoor sanctuary spreads memorials, stonework and worship spaces across a hill facing Mount Monadnock. Its centerpiece is a massive open-air altar assembled as a memorial to Americans who died in military service. The grounds are generally open dawn to dusk year-round, although staffed facilities have more limited hours.', 'open', 'https://www.cathedralofthepines.org/', 'https://www.cathedralofthepines.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Panarchy Tomb Room', 'panarchy-tomb-room', 'weird-history', 43.70148, -72.29148, 'Hanover', 'NH', 'The Panarchy undergraduate society occupies a former fraternity house containing a basement room decorated like a ritual chamber, complete with a stone tomb-like centerpiece. The unusual interior has become an online curiosity, but Panarchy is a private residential society rather than a public attraction. OddWay visitors should treat this as an exterior-only history stop and should not attempt to enter.', 'private', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/panarchy-tomb-room', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Aleister Crowley''s Magickal Retirement Cabin', 'aleister-crowleys-magickal-retirement-cabin', 'haunted', 43.69435, -71.80538, 'Hebron', 'NH', 'Occultist Aleister Crowley spent several months in Hebron in 1916 during what he described as a magickal retirement. The small house associated with that period still survives, giving New Hampshire a direct physical connection to one of the twentieth century''s most notorious occult figures. It is a private residence and should be viewed only from a lawful public road.', 'private', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/aleister-crowley-s-magickal-retirement', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Stone Tower', 'stone-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 43.95061, -71.5049, 'Waterville Valley', 'NH', 'This stone tower looks like the romantic ruin of an ancient structure, but that appearance was intentional from the beginning. Reverend J.M. Buckley reportedly decided the valley had nearly every scenic feature except a ruin and built one to complete the landscape. A trail from the Waterville Valley area reaches the deliberately fake relic.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-stone-tower', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Abandoned Train Cars of Bartlett', 'abandoned-train-cars-of-bartlett', 'weird-history', 44.07768, -71.28004, 'Bartlett', 'NH', 'Several aging rail cars and a locomotive have long sat near the old Mountain Division rail corridor in Bartlett, creating the appearance of a forgotten train left in the woods. Their condition and exact access can change as rail and property work evolves. Follow current signage and lawful local access, stay off any active tracks, and do not climb into or damage the equipment.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-abandoned-train-cars-of-bartlett-nh', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Zimmerman House', 'zimmerman-house', 'roadside-oddities', 43.02172, -71.46287, 'Manchester', 'NH', 'Frank Lloyd Wright designed the Zimmerman House as a compact Usonian home tailored closely to its owners, furnishings and landscape. The Currier Museum of Art now operates guided tours, giving visitors a rare chance to enter an intact Wright residence rather than only viewing it from outside. Tours are ticketed and depart under museum procedures; do not wander the residential neighborhood expecting independent access.', 'limited', 'https://www.currier.org/frank-lloyd-wright', 'https://www.currier.org/frank-lloyd-wright', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Nansen Ski Jump', 'nansen-ski-jump', 'weird-history', 44.53068, -71.16444, 'Milan', 'NH', 'The enormous Nansen Ski Jump rises above the North Country like an industrial skeleton built into the hillside. Completed in the 1930s, it hosted major competitions and Olympic trials and was once among the largest ski jumps in the eastern United States. The state historic site preserves the structure and surrounding grounds, but visitors should obey barriers and never climb the tower.', 'open', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/nansen-ski-jump-state-historic-site', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Parrish Shoes Jumanji Sign', 'parrish-shoes-jumanji-sign', 'weird-history', 42.93365, -72.27865, 'Keene', 'NH', 'Downtown Keene stood in for the fictional town of Brantford in the 1995 film "Jumanji." A Parrish Shoes sign connected to the movie was later recreated and became a local memorial to Robin Williams after his death. The sign remains an easy public stop for fans of the film.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/parrish-shoes-sign', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Ice Castles', 'ice-castles', 'roadside-oddities', 44.03438, -71.69884, 'North Woodstock', 'NH', 'Each winter, crews build a walk-through landscape from hundreds of thousands of icicles and massive frozen walls. Tunnels, towers, slides and illuminated chambers change shape as the weather changes, making the attraction temporary by design. Opening dates depend heavily on winter conditions and tickets can sell out.', 'limited', 'https://icecastles.com/new-hampshire/', 'https://icecastles.com/new-hampshire/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Yankee Siege Trebuchet', 'yankee-siege-trebuchet', 'roadside-oddities', 42.95431, -71.92173, 'Greenfield', 'NH', 'This giant six-story trebuchet was built to hurl pumpkins hundreds of feet during the era of competitive pumpkin chunking. Yankee Siege retired from regular operation in 2010 but remains an enormous reminder of one of New England''s stranger engineering hobbies. It is on private property with no-trespassing restrictions, so OddWay should treat it as roadside-view-only.', 'private', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/yankee-siege-trebuchet', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Steps to Nowhere', 'steps-to-nowhere', 'weird-history', 43.2006, -71.53348, 'Concord', 'NH', 'Two stone staircases stand without a house, leading upward into empty space beside a Concord street. They are remnants of the final home of President Franklin Pierce, which survived long after his death before being demolished in the twentieth century. The stairs are a compact physical ghost of a building that no longer exists.', 'roadside', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/steps-to-nowhere', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Gravesite of Dixville''s First Settlers', 'gravesite-of-dixvilles-first-settlers', 'weird-history', 44.85643, -71.28597, 'Dixville', 'NH', 'A tiny burial site near Dixville Notch preserves the story of early settler Betsey Whittemore, who died in December 1815. Winter conditions were so severe that her body reportedly could not be transported out of the notch and had to remain until burial became possible. The graves are near the public waterfall parking area but should be treated as a cemetery, not a roadside prop.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/gravesite-of-dixvilles-first-settlers', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Colebrook Murder Victims Memorial', 'colebrook-murder-victims-memorial', 'weird-history', 44.89496, -71.49688, 'Colebrook', 'NH', 'This memorial honors four people killed during Carl Drega''s 1997 shooting rampage in Colebrook: two New Hampshire state troopers, a judge and a newspaper editor. The monument gives visitors a concrete place to understand a violent event that deeply affected the North Country community. OddWay should present it strictly as a respectful memorial.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/colebrook-murder-victims-memorial', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Republic of Indian Stream Historical Marker', 'republic-of-indian-stream-historical-marker', 'weird-history', 45.05152, -71.38706, 'Pittsburg', 'NH', 'For several years in the 1830s, residents north of Pittsburg organized the self-declared Republic of Indian Stream amid a border dispute between the United States and British Canada. The tiny government had its own constitution and local institutions before the territory was absorbed into New Hampshire. A state marker on U.S. Route 3 commemorates the unlikely republic. Coordinate source: https://mm.nh.gov/files/uploads/dhr/documents/highway-markers-by-number.pdf', 'roadside', 'https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2014-01-24/marking-history-republic-of-indian-stream-in-pittsburg', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Site of the Pine Tree Riot', 'site-of-the-pine-tree-riot', 'weird-history', 43.05226, -71.70555, 'Weare', 'NH', 'In 1772, New Hampshire mill owners resisted royal officials attempting to enforce laws reserving the colony''s largest white pines for the British Crown. The confrontation became known as the Pine Tree Riot and is often remembered as an early act of resistance preceding the American Revolution. A marker and millstone identify the historic tavern site.', 'roadside', 'https://www.wearehistoricalsociety.org/pineriot.php', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Chicken Farmer Rock', 'chicken-farmer-rock', 'folklore', 43.29656, -71.99594, 'Newbury', 'NH', 'For decades, a roadside boulder has carried the hand-painted message "Chicken Farmer, I Still Love You." Local versions of the story connect it to a long-ago romance, but the exact origin has become part fact and part community folklore. The rock is visible from the road; visitors should not stop in traffic or enter private property for a photograph.', 'roadside', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/chicken-farmer-rock', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Uncle Sam House', 'uncle-sam-house', 'weird-history', 42.72814, -71.76323, 'Mason', 'NH', 'Samuel Wilson, the meatpacker traditionally associated with the American "Uncle Sam" nickname, spent part of his early life in this Mason house. The exact development of the national symbol is more complicated than the popular legend suggests, but Wilson''s connection has been officially commemorated. The house is private property, so view the marker and exterior only from a lawful public area.', 'private', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-uncle-sam-house-mason-new-hampshire', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Northfield Drive-In Theater', 'northfield-drive-in-theater', 'weird-history', 42.72724, -72.44959, 'Hinsdale', 'NH', 'The Northfield Drive-In sits directly along the New Hampshire–Massachusetts state line, and its unusual placement is tied to historic differences in movie-projection labor rules. The drive-in also appeared in the film "The Cider House Rules." It continues to operate seasonally, so check the current movie schedule before routing here.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/northfield-drive-in-theater', 'https://www.northfielddrivein.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Dixville Notch Midnight Voting Site — The Balsams', 'dixville-notch-midnight-voting-site-the-balsams', 'weird-history', 44.88172, -71.31662, 'Dixville', 'NH', 'Dixville Notch became nationally famous for casting presidential-primary and general-election ballots just after midnight, traditionally inside The Balsams resort. The tiny community''s first-results ritual became one of New Hampshire''s strangest political traditions. The historic hotel has been closed while redevelopment plans continue, so this is an exterior and historical-routing stop only unless public access is officially announced.', 'private', 'https://www.historic-structures.com/nh/dixville/balsams_resort.php', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('African Burying Ground Memorial Park', 'african-burying-ground-memorial-park', 'weird-history', 43.07513, -70.75903, 'Portsmouth', 'NH', 'Construction work in 2003 uncovered human remains beneath Chestnut Street, revealing a forgotten eighteenth-century African burial ground. Archaeological work identified multiple individuals of African descent, and the city later created a public memorial park over the site. It is a solemn burial and remembrance space and should be treated accordingly.', 'open', 'https://www.portsmouthnh.gov/publicworks/portsmouth-african-burying-ground-memorial-park', 'https://africanburyinggroundnh.org/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Yoken''s Whale Neon Sign', 'yokens-whale-neon-sign', 'roadside-oddities', 43.0451, -70.77305, 'Portsmouth', 'NH', 'A restored neon whale once advertised Yoken''s restaurant, a longtime Portsmouth-area seafood landmark. Although the restaurant itself disappeared, the glowing whale was preserved and returned to the old property as a piece of roadside Americana. It is especially striking after dark and can be viewed from public roadside areas.', 'roadside', 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/61603', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Lizzie Bourne Memorial', 'lizzie-bourne-memorial', 'weird-history', 44.2721, -71.30205, 'Jackson', 'NH', 'A stone memorial near the summit of Mount Washington marks where 23-year-old Lizzie Bourne died from exposure during a storm in September 1855. She was only a short distance from shelter when she died, and the location became a lasting warning about the mountain''s rapidly changing weather. There is no clear safe public footpath to the monument; the safest way to view it is from the Mount Washington Cog Railway as it passes nearby.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/lizzie-bourne-memorial', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Frankenstein Cliff Trailhead', 'frankenstein-cliff-trailhead', 'roadside-oddities', 44.14781, -71.36781, 'Hart''s Location', 'NH', 'Frankenstein Cliff rises dramatically above Crawford Notch and is reached as part of a steep hiking loop near Arethusa Falls. Despite the horror-movie association the name suggests, the cliff honors nineteenth-century landscape painter Godfrey Frankenstein rather than Mary Shelley''s creature. The coordinate routes to the established trailhead rather than to the cliff face itself. Trail source: https://www.trailfinder.info/trails/trail/crawford-notch-state-park-frankenstein-cliff-loop', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/frankenstein-cliff', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Contoocook Railroad Covered Bridge', 'contoocook-railroad-covered-bridge', 'roadside-oddities', 43.2231, -71.71387, 'Contoocook', 'NH', 'This long wooden bridge was built for railroad traffic rather than wagons or automobiles and survives as one of the country''s oldest covered railroad bridges. Its heavy timber trusses once carried trains across the Contoocook River. Today the preserved structure can be explored on foot from public areas.', 'open', 'https://www.new.coveredbridges.net/new-hampshire-bridges/contoocook', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Weeks Estate', 'weeks-estate', 'roadside-oddities', 44.45028, -71.57111, 'Lancaster', 'NH', 'Former U.S. senator John Wingate Weeks built this mountaintop estate with a mansion, stone observation tower and carefully planned grounds overlooking the White Mountains. The house preserves period rooms and collections while the tower provides a striking landmark above Lancaster. Vehicle access, house tours and tower openings follow a seasonal state-park schedule, while trail access is broader.', 'limited', 'https://www.nhstateparks.org/find-parks-trails/weeks-state-park', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Clark''s Bears', 'clarks-bears', 'roadside-oddities', 44.04833, -71.68556, 'Lincoln', 'NH', 'Clark''s has operated as a White Mountains roadside attraction for generations, combining trained bear shows, the White Mountain Central Railroad and a collection of intentionally old-fashioned amusements. Its mix of live animals, steam trains and roadside-showmanship history makes it a distinctly New Hampshire oddity. The attraction is ticketed and seasonal.', 'limited', 'https://www.clarksbears.com/detailsAdmission.php', 'https://www.clarksbears.com/', 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Milford Swing Bridge', 'milford-swing-bridge', 'roadside-oddities', 42.83655, -71.64569, 'Milford', 'NH', 'A narrow iron suspension footbridge crosses the Souhegan River in Milford, swaying noticeably as pedestrians move across it. The current bridge dates to the nineteenth century and feels more like a miniature Victorian suspension bridge than a typical town walkway. It remains a pedestrian crossing, so visitors can experience the movement directly.', 'open', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-swing-bridge', null, 'America/New_York', now()),
  ('Garnet Pool', 'garnet-pool', 'roadside-oddities', 44.30312, -71.22119, 'Greens', 'NH', 'Garnet Pool was once promoted as a scenic Victorian-era swimming hole near Mount Washington before fading from mainstream tourist maps. The secluded pool and surrounding rock formations survive without the formal infrastructure of a modern attraction. There is no clearly signed official trail, conditions can be slippery, and the source warns that common map directions can be wrong, so visitors should use caution and avoid treating it as a guaranteed swimming stop.', 'limited', 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/garnet-pools', null, 'America/New_York', now())
on conflict (slug) do update set
  description   = excluded.description,
  public_access = excluded.public_access,
  source        = excluded.source,
  website       = excluded.website,
  verified_at   = excluded.verified_at;

select count(*) as nh_stops from public.stops where state = 'NH';
